{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20168",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.55,
      "end_seconds": 3.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Sorry I'm a little late, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.03,
      "end_seconds": 8.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Right, come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.05,
      "end_seconds": 15.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "Good morning, uh, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.89,
      "end_seconds": 19.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.86,
      "end_seconds": 26.05,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "yeah, it's a dry cough i don't know what's causing it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.58,
      "end_seconds": 28.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.45,
      "end_seconds": 41.97,
      "duration_seconds": 12.52,
      "text": "Mm, I've had it for about a week. I did try to ignore it for a while. My neighbour said I should get it looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.57,
      "end_seconds": 47.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.31,
      "end_seconds": 52.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "It happens a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.54,
      "end_seconds": 55.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Okay, go on. Does anything help it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.41,
      "end_seconds": 61.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Actually, only honey, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.52,
      "end_seconds": 67.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "So, rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.09,
      "end_seconds": 69.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Moderate, I'd say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.41,
      "end_seconds": 80.58,
      "duration_seconds": 10.17,
      "text": "Um, um, and the the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 80.68,
      "end_seconds": 85.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.55,
      "end_seconds": 106.63,
      "duration_seconds": 19.08,
      "text": "I was getting to that! I've also had a high temperature, since last Tuesday as for high temperature, honestly, once or twice a day oh, and loss of taste had that since this morning with loss of taste, moderate, really"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.16,
      "end_seconds": 114.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "Have you had a dry cough before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.15,
      "end_seconds": 123.53,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "Right, yes, something like this happened last winter, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.83,
      "end_seconds": 127.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.26,
      "end_seconds": 129.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.71,
      "end_seconds": 131.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "look straight ahead"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.79,
      "end_seconds": 150.33,
      "duration_seconds": 9.54,
      "text": "Your chest is clear apart from a few crackles at the right base and your oxygen level is a bit low."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.49,
      "end_seconds": 161.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "You can sit up now. Any confusion, leg swelling or blue lips at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.22,
      "end_seconds": 178.38,
      "duration_seconds": 16.16,
      "text": "um, no, no confusion, no leg swelling, no blue lips i did have aching all over at one point, but that that went away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.31,
      "end_seconds": 182.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "any chest pain or vomiting at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.04,
      "end_seconds": 186.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "no, no chest pain or vomiting"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.73,
      "end_seconds": 190.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Right, any sign of diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.74,
      "end_seconds": 193.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "No diarrhoea, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 194.32,
      "end_seconds": 200.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "Actually, you know, doctor, I did notice diarrhoea. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.3,
      "end_seconds": 207.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.45,
      "end_seconds": 215.54,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.58,
      "end_seconds": 219.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.61,
      "end_seconds": 225.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.92,
      "end_seconds": 236.85,
      "duration_seconds": 9.93,
      "text": "Yes, nickel. I get a rash on my skin. Yeah, you know, I'm allergic to kiwi, I get hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.28,
      "end_seconds": 239.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "right, what about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.21,
      "end_seconds": 244.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.75,
      "end_seconds": 247.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.18,
      "end_seconds": 250.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.09,
      "end_seconds": 253.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "So, what's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.68,
      "end_seconds": 258.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.42,
      "end_seconds": 264.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 265.45,
      "end_seconds": 278.41,
      "duration_seconds": 12.96,
      "text": "it's glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast, doctor. She is on ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure, I give it to her"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.1,
      "end_seconds": 280.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Is that long-standing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 280.8,
      "end_seconds": 291.36,
      "duration_seconds": 10.56,
      "text": "About two months. Um, it's Tiotropium inhaler, once a day, doctor. It's Dolo, 650 milligrams, when I get the fever, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.17,
      "end_seconds": 297.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "So, before this I was on glibenclamide; that's been stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.21,
      "end_seconds": 312.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.74,
      "end_seconds": 317.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for about a year now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.98,
      "end_seconds": 320.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Is that everything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.71,
      "end_seconds": 333.87,
      "duration_seconds": 12.16,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure, yes. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. Well, I've had COPD, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.88,
      "end_seconds": 360.51,
      "duration_seconds": 25.63,
      "text": "Yes, COPD is known to us, good to have that clear. So, based on the history and the examination, I'd lean towards a viral chest infection with mildly low oxygen. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. We shouldn't forget a flare of heart failure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.09,
      "end_seconds": 363.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.18,
      "end_seconds": 374.99,
      "duration_seconds": 9.81,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a viral chest infection with mildly low oxygen do well once it's treated properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.09,
      "end_seconds": 393.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "I'll request a viral swab, it'll help with fever and cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 394.6,
      "end_seconds": 399.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "We have a slot Wednesday at 2 pm, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.19,
      "end_seconds": 421.18,
      "duration_seconds": 19.99,
      "text": "Let's get a chest X-ray, for low oxygen and crackles. Rest, keep your fluids up and lie on your tummy or side to help your breathing. If you become more breathless or confused, that's the point to come in urgently. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 421.86,
      "end_seconds": 425.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 427.35,
      "end_seconds": 428.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "have a good day"
    }
  ]
}